# Build toolchain: Kivy is COMPILED here, not downloaded.
#
# RUNTIME-INVENTORY.md, the single most consequential finding: the installed
# Kivy-2.3.1.dist-info/WHEEL reads "Tag: cp313-cp313-linux_armv7l" and NO SUCH
# WHEEL EXISTS ON PyPI. It was built from sdist on the device. ospi never pays
# this cost -- on its Python version rotary-controller-python pulls a prebuilt
# wheel -- which is why its stage installs runtime SDL2 only.
#
# build-essential, pkg-config and python3-venv already come from upstream
# stage2/01-sys-tweaks; the -dev set does not.

libsdl2-dev
libsdl2-image-dev
libsdl2-mixer-dev
libsdl2-ttf-dev
libmtdev-dev
python3-dev

# Present via stage2, named here because the Kivy build fails without them and
# the harness asserts on this contract.
build-essential
pkg-config

# Cython arrives transiently through PEP 517 build isolation. It is deliberately
# NOT installed as a package -- it is not one on the live machine either.
